    user: "Unsa ang electromagnetic spectrum?",
    assistant: "Nindot kaayo nga pangutana! Ang electromagnetic spectrum mao ang complete range sa tanan nga electromagnetic radiation, gi-arrange base sa wavelength o frequency.\n\n**Basic Concepts:**\n\nAng electromagnetic waves mga transverse waves nga adunay oscillating electric ug magnetic fields. Sila makatravel sa vacuum (dili kinahanglan og medium) sa speed of light (c = 300,000 km/s).\n\nAng relationship tali sa wavelength (λ), frequency (f), ug speed (c):\nc = λ × f\n\nKung ang wavelength motaas, ang frequency mohunong (inverse relationship).\n\n**Ang Electromagnetic Spectrum (gikan sa longest wavelength/lowest frequency ngadto sa shortest wavelength/highest frequency):**\n\n1. **Radio Waves** (λ > 1 m)\n- Longest wavelength, lowest frequency ug energy\n- Applications: AM/FM radio, television, WiFi, Bluetooth, cell phones, radar\n- Safe: Dili makadaot sa human body sa normal exposure levels\n\n2. **Microwaves** (1 mm - 1 m)\n- Applications: Microwave ovens, satellite communications, GPS, cell phone signals\n- Safety: Makapainit sa tissues (mao nga gigamit sa cooking), pero generally safe sa controlled amounts\n\n3. **Infrared (IR)** (700 nm - 1 mm)\n- 'Below red' - dili makita pero mabati isip heat\n- Applications: Remote controls, thermal imaging, heat lamps, night vision goggles\n- Natural source: Ang tanan nga butang nga adunay temperature nag-emit og infrared\n\n4. **Visible Light** (400-700 nm)\n- Ang bugtong parte sa spectrum nga makita sa human eye\n- Kolor gikan sa longest wavelength ngadto sa shortest: Red, Orange, Yellow, Green, Blue, Indigo, Violet (ROYGBIV)\n- Applications: Vision, photography, fiber optics, lasers\n\n5. **Ultraviolet (UV)** (10-400 nm)\n- 'Beyond violet' - dili makita\n- Natural source: Sunlight\n- Applications: Sterilization, black lights, forensics, vitamin D production\n- DANGER: Makadaot sa skin (sunburn, skin cancer) ug eyes (cataracts)\n- Types: UVA (aging), UVB (burning), UVC (most dangerous, pero gi-absorb sa ozone layer)\n\n6. **X-rays** (0.01-10 nm)\n- High energy, makapenetrate sa soft tissues pero gi-absorb sa dense materials (bones)\n- Applications: Medical imaging (X-ray radiography), airport security scanners, crystallography\n- DANGER: Ionizing radiation - makadaot sa DNA, makapahinabo og cancer\n- Safety: Minimal exposure, protective shielding\n\n7. **Gamma Rays** (< 0.01 nm)\n- Shortest wavelength, highest frequency ug energy\n- Sources: Nuclear reactions, radioactive decay, supernovae, black holes\n- Applications: Cancer treatment (radiation therapy), sterilization sa medical equipment, food irradiation\n- DANGER: Highly ionizing, very dangerous sa living tissues\n- Safety: Heavy shielding (lead, concrete), strict exposure limits\n\n**Ionizing vs Non-Ionizing Radiation:**\n\n- **Non-ionizing** (Radio, Microwave, IR, Visible): Dili igo ang energy para mag-remove og electrons sa atoms. Generally safe sa normal exposure.\n- **Ionizing** (UV, X-ray, Gamma): Igo ang energy para mag-remove og electrons, makadaot sa DNA ug cells. Dangerous, kinahanglan og precautions.\n\n**Applications sa Daily Life:**\n\n- Communication: Radio, TV, cell phones, WiFi (radio waves ug microwaves)\n- Medicine: X-rays, CT scans, radiation therapy\n- Cooking: Microwave ovens\n- Security: Airport scanners, night vision\n- Astronomy: Tanan nga wavelengths gigamit para mag-observe sa universe (radio telescopes, X-ray telescopes)\n\nSa Pilipinas, ang electromagnetic spectrum regulated sa National Telecommunications Commission (NTC). Ang different frequencies gi-allocate sa different users (broadcasting, telecommunications, military, scientific research).\n\nAng sunlight nga moabot sa Earth adunay UV, visible, ug infrared radiation. Ang ozone layer nag-block sa dangerous UVC ug kadaghanan sa UVB, nag-protect kanato.\n\nSa imong hunahuna, unsang parte sa electromagnetic spectrum ang labing importante sa modernong komunikasyon ug ngano?"
